Z||000011||Raydar||12-04-1999||09:34 PM||||Okay, I'm curious... Has anyone ever heard of a lawsuit being filed on the grounds that IR laser energy (LIDAR), shined at oncoming traffic, might be dangerous to the eyes? <BR>I am fairly familiar with the technology, and recognize that the chance of injury is very small, but considering some of the lawsuits that I hear about on the news, I'm surprised that nobody has tried this. A dedicated speeder (speeders? class action?!?) could possibly keep this tied up in court for years. Merely my own crackpot observation.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
