Z||000016||DJRice||12-06-1999||08:57 AM||||This is deviating from the topic a bit, but I  worked for a place that sold Radar Detectors, and you would be surprised at the amount of people who dont know exactly what these things do.  On several occasions, I had people buy them, keep them for a week or so, and then return them because they "Had passed several police cars, and the thing never made a noise."<P>Well, Duh.  Its designed to detect Radar or Laser, not police.  HeHe||||reg||10
Z||000017||88 Fiero||12-06-1999||03:38 PM||||There was an article on Car and Driver...March 1996 regarding Jammers for Radar.. There were 7 Jammers available and was compared and tested along with the metropolitan police...Out of this Radar Jammers the "Remote Systems ECm 5446 outperformed the other brands...The designer was Steve Fong who was a former Escort Radar Detector designer.. The only thing tho on his radar is that he cannot sell you a complete unit.. He will sell you a plan how to build one and cost would probably around $1,700.00 at that time.. I don't know how much is it now. As far as Laser Guns...If you are driving a bright color car...and speeding. And a cop uses a laser gun on you...chances are the laser will reflect on your car's color and bounce back to it's unit and will give them a reading...so expect to be pulled over. But if you are driving a car with a black color..you've got a better chance of getting away with it beecause once a laser gun aim at you the beam will be absorb by the dark color and will not reflect back... also...if you have alot of reflective lensesit  can cause for a laser gun to detect you...the less lense for reflection the better...advantage of our car is that one..our headlightsare  pop-up and the turn signals are too small for a laser gun to be aimed at in a distance..and if the car is painted black...it will be a piece of cake... ( as long as it is a laser gun)....but then once you passed that point and the rear of car with that big taillight lense (GT's)..then something to think about..maybe slow down....<p>[This message has been edited by 88 Fiero (edited 12-06-1999).]||||reg||10
Z||000018||Tom88gt||01-21-2000||04:05 PM||||Any "passive" jammer is bogus.  You will need an active one.  Since it is illegal to jam a legal transmission (radar, tv, radio, etc) you can't sell or buy such equipment (unless you are the government, ie modern day Nazis).<P>However, the information and individual parts needed to build one are not illegal.  You just need the info and supplies.  There are a few companies/individuals who do sell the real thing, minus a transmitter or other readily available, but key part.  <P>Just don't get caught with your new toy.  <P>For laser, you need IR to jam the laser guns IR beam.  Basically you confuse it.  Your headlights (not ideal for a Fiero) will work to some degree since they do put out IR light.  High beams are best.  But in the daytime your headlights give a long range warning to the cop that you are coming.  If you could figure out how to filter out the visible part of the lights and not affect the IR that would be better.  A powerfull set of foglights with filters would be ideal.  Also, skip the front license plate (favorite target) or buy a "laser jamming" plastic cover.  The worst that will happen is the cop will tell you to put your plate back on or remnove the cover.  5 min later just reverse it again.||||reg||1
Z||000019||DRH||01-21-2000||04:45 PM||||Wisconsin uses a lot of VASCAR. I don't remember what the whole acronym stands for but the V is "Visual". It's basically a stop watch that times you over a known distance and computes the speed. The only input is the nice officer punches the button at the (hopefully) appropriate time. NO radar/laser detector/jammer will do you any good.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Now... if I could only get my hands on a Klingon cloaking device...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
